title: Social Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: social_welfare_timer = 10; month_actions += 1
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and social_welfare_timer = 0
card-image: img/portraits/JuchaczMarie.jpg

= Social Policy

Pensions, the Grundsicherung, health and long-term care are the heart of the German welfare state, and much of it was built by Social Democrats. There is constant pressure to cut it[? if recession_seen = 1 :, especially now that the economy is in trouble ?].

- @reduce_spending: Reduce social spending.
- @increase_spending_normal: Increase social spending.
- @increase_spending_crisis: Increase spending (benefits will stay about the same).
- @spending_same_normal: Keep spending the same.
- @spending_same_crisis: Keep spending the same (in effect a cut).
- @easy_discard

@reduce_spending
subtitle: This will hurt our core voters. +1 Budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: welfare >= -5
on-arrival: budget += 1; workers_spd -= 6; unemployed_spd -= 6; workers_linke += 3; welfare -= 1; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5; fdp_relation += 5; cdu_relation += 3; trust_in_democracy -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1 if in_grand_coalition and coalition_dissent > 0; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; linke_relation -= 8; inflation -= 0.3; unemployment_rate += 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.2;

We cut social spending. Our critics say that we are making the poorest pay for a budget we could have balanced in other ways. Many of our voters agree with them.

@increase_spending_normal
view-if: unemployment_rate <= 8
choose-if: budget > 0
subtitle: -1 Budget
on-arrival: budget -= 1; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); welfare += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare > 1; welfare_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.3; unemployment_rate -= 0.4; economic_growth += 0.2;

We raise pensions and the Grundsicherung. Our core voters are pleased.

@increase_spending_crisis
view-if: unemployment_rate > 8
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: budget -= 1; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare > 0; welfare_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.3
subtitle: With more people out of work, it takes more money just to keep benefits where they are. -1 Budget

With unemployment this high, more spending only keeps benefits where they are. We are treading water.

@spending_same_normal
view-if: unemployment_rate <= 8

We keep social spending the same.

@spending_same_crisis
view-if: unemployment_rate > 8
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 4; welfare -= 1; reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; linke_relation -= 8 if in_left_front
subtitle: With more people out of work, the same budget means lower benefits.

With more people out of work, the same budget means lower benefits for each of them. Our voters notice.

[? if in_left_front: The Linke is turning against us over our social policy. ?]
